# Agent Blueprint Protocol cheatsheet

This reference is for developers using the Elixir or TypeScript facade. It lists the common calls for decoding, encoding, reconciling, and running conformance.

## Elixir facade

### Decode artifacts

Excerpt. Provide the artifact bytes before running these calls.

```elixir
{:ok, blueprint} = AgentBlueprintProtocol.decode_blueprint(blueprint_bytes)
{:ok, deployment} = AgentBlueprintProtocol.decode_deployment(deployment_bytes)
{:ok, envelope} = AgentBlueprintProtocol.decode_federation_envelope(envelope_bytes)
```

### Encode and compute identity

Excerpt. `blueprint` is a decoded Blueprint.

```elixir
{:ok, canonical_bytes} = AgentBlueprintProtocol.canonical_bytes(blueprint)
digest = AgentBlueprintProtocol.Blueprint.content_digest(blueprint)
tagged_digest = AgentBlueprintProtocol.Digest.to_tagged(digest)
```

### Reconcile artifacts

Excerpt. Supply host bounds, revision support, keys, and observations in an `AgentBlueprintProtocol.Reconcile.Inputs` struct.

```elixir
{:ok, evidence} = AgentBlueprintProtocol.reconcile(blueprint, deployment, inputs)
```

### Run the corpus

From a checkout of the repository:

```sh
mix conformance.verify
```

## TypeScript facade

### Import package-root functions

Excerpt. Provide byte arrays and inputs from your application.

```ts
import {
  canonicalBytes,
  decodeBlueprint,
  decodeDeployment,
  decodeFederationEnvelope,
  reconcile
} from "@agent-blueprint-protocol/verifier";

const blueprint = decodeBlueprint(blueprintBytes);
const deployment = decodeDeployment(deploymentBytes);
const envelope = decodeFederationEnvelope(envelopeBytes);
if (blueprint.ok && deployment.ok) {
  const result = reconcile(blueprint.value, deployment.value, inputs);
}
```

### Run the embedded corpus

```sh
npx @agent-blueprint-protocol/verifier@1.0.0-rc.2
```

### Run an external implementation

Command template (excerpt). Replace `./example-adapter` with the adapter executable supplied by the implementation.

```sh
npx @agent-blueprint-protocol/verifier@1.0.0-rc.2 conformance run --corpus ./conformance --results results.json -- ./example-adapter
```

Cost amounts are integer millionths of the named currency unit. Verification returns evidence and does not grant permission to act.

